sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor App as Application
    participant Client as MqttSessionClient
    participant Broker as MQTT broker

    Note over Client,Broker: An MQTT session is durable protocol state identified by Client ID
    App->>Client: Connect with initial Clean Start choice
    Client->>Broker: CONNECT<br/>Clean Start = true or false<br/>Session Expiry > 0
    Broker-->>Client: CONNACK<br/>Session Present says whether an old session resumed
    Note over Client: Start local request workers

    App->>Client: Publish, Subscribe, or Unsubscribe
    Client->>Broker: MQTT request
    Broker--xClient: TCP, TLS, or MQTT connection is lost
    Note over Client: Pause request workers<br/>Keep pending outgoing requests<br/>Clear queued acknowledgements for received publishes

    Client->>Broker: Reconnect with same Client ID<br/>Clean Start = false
    alt Broker retained the unexpired session
        Broker-->>Client: CONNACK<br/>Session Present = true
        Note over Broker: Existing subscriptions and queued QoS state remain
        Note over Client: Resume pending local requests
    else Broker no longer has the session
        Broker-->>Client: CONNACK<br/>Session Present = false
        Client->>Broker: DISCONNECT<br/>Session Expiry = 0
        Client-->>App: Fatal session-lost notification
    end

    opt Application deliberately closes a live session
        App->>Client: Disconnect
        Client->>Broker: DISCONNECT<br/>Session Expiry = 0
        Note over Client,Broker: Stop reconnecting and delete broker-side session state
    end